DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260803T110000
SUMMARY:MiM: Day-1 software setup (one time)
DESCRIPTION:One-time account setup. Do it once\, never touch again.\n\nDO
 \n- Create the 4 accounts on annual billing (Riverside Pro\, Descript Cr
 eator\, Transistor Pro\, Calendly Standard).\n- In Riverside\, enable 'E
 xport to Descript' (email Riverside support now if the button is missing
 ).\n- Connect the YouTube channel inside Transistor (document the manual
 -upload fallback if it won't connect).\n- Publish a 60-second TRAILER no
 w and submit the RSS feed to Apple Podcasts Connect and Spotify for Crea
 tors (Apple's and Spotify's podcast submission sites)\, so directory rev
 iew (days\, sometimes weeks) clears well before launch.\n- Run one priva
 te/unlisted end-to-end test episode: Transistor -> confirm Apple/Spotify
  ingest + YouTube auto-post actually fire.\n- Build the Calendly 'Record
 ing' event (75 min\, 15-min buffers\, Riverside link as location\, 3 int
 ake questions)\; confirm the invite carries the link and the prep doc re
 solves view-only.\n- Write the guest prep one-pager (Google Doc\, view-o
 nly).\n- Set up the shared master-asset cloud folder (Drive/Dropbox)\, o
 ne folder per episode.\n- Add both Rich and Carla as admins on each acco
 unt where allowed\; record logins in a credentials note.\n- Confirm edit
 or lanes: Rich owns the cut/multicam/export\; Carla owns clip selection 
 + caption QA + guest-clip send.\n\nRIGHT LOOKS LIKE\n- Accounts live + b
 oth admins\; trailer published and feeds submitted for early review\; pr
 ivate end-to-end publish proven\; YouTube connected\; Calendly + prep do
 c verified\; shared asset folder ready.\n\nHOW-TO GUIDES (plain language
 \, jargon decoded\, each with a chatbot prompt)\n- Day-1 setup\, step by
  step: https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/blob/main/how-t
 o/day1-setup.md\n- All guides: https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-i
 n-motion/blob/main/how-to/README.md\n\nASSISTANT PROMPT (paste into Clau
 de or ChatGPT for step-by-step help)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in 
 Motion\, the AES podcast: a remote\, two-host video interview show that 
 turns Amazon's internal operating mechanisms into playbooks any company 
 can use (tagline 'Day 1 Energy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns lo
 gistics\; Carla owns the guest slate. Today's step: One-time account set
 up. Do it once\, never touch again. WHAT TO DO: (1) Create the 4 account
 s on annual billing (Riverside Pro\, Descript Creator\, Transistor Pro\,
  Calendly Standard). (2) In Riverside\, enable 'Export to Descript' (ema
 il Riverside support now if the button is missing). (3) Connect the YouT
 ube channel inside Transistor (document the manual-upload fallback if it
  won't connect). (4) Publish a 60-second TRAILER now and submit the RSS 
 feed to Apple Podcasts Connect and Spotify for Creators (Apple's and Spo
 tify's podcast submission sites)\, so directory review (days\, sometimes
  weeks) clears well before launch. (5) Run one private/unlisted end-to-e
 nd test episode: Transistor -> confirm Apple/Spotify ingest + YouTube au
 to-post actually fire. (6) Build the Calendly 'Recording' event (75 min\
 , 15-min buffers\, Riverside link as location\, 3 intake questions)\; co
 nfirm the invite carries the link and the prep doc resolves view-only. (
 7) Write the guest prep one-pager (Google Doc\, view-only). (8) Set up t
 he shared master-asset cloud folder (Drive/Dropbox)\, one folder per epi
 sode. (9) Add both Rich and Carla as admins on each account where allowe
 d\; record logins in a credentials note. (10) Confirm editor lanes: Rich
  owns the cut/multicam/export\; Carla owns clip selection + caption QA +
  guest-clip send. DONE WHEN: Accounts live + both admins\; trailer publi
 shed and feeds submitted for early review\; private end-to-end publish p
 roven\; YouTube connected\; Calendly + prep doc verified\; shared asset 
 folder ready.. YOUR TASK: We are at STEP 6: Day-1 software setup. Give m
 e an ordered runbook with the exact click-path for each task\, the trail
 er + private-test-episode procedure\, the precise Calendly 'Recording' f
 ields\, and the full text of the guest prep one-pager (include a one-lin
 e audio+video reuse consent).\n\nFULL PROJECT SPEC (optional\, for deep 
 context): https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-moti
 on/main/mim-assistant-context.md
