UID:mim-test-run@mechanismsinmotion.aes
DTSTAMP:20260603T160000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260813T094500
SUMMARY:MiM: Full test run (Rich + Carla + stand-in guest)
LOCATION:Riverside studio link (paste the persistent studio URL here once
  created)
DESCRIPTION:Prove the whole chain AND rehearse the real failure modes bef
 ore the first marquee guest. Costs nothing to break here.\n\nDO\n- Rich 
 + Carla + a stand-in on a RANDOM laptop with a default webcam (rehearse 
 the degraded guest\, not the happy path).\n- Mid-record\, have the stand
 -in close the tab and rejoin\; confirm their local track survived.\n- Co
 nfirm every participant's tracks upload to 100%\; rehearse the fix for a
  guest whose camera recorded at an odd frame rate (converting it to a st
 eady 30fps\, called CFR / constant frame rate\; the descript-edit guide 
 has the one-click fix).\n- Export to Descript\; confirm each person land
 s as a SEPARATE track\; verify lip-sync at the END of the take.\n- Confi
 rm 30fps everywhere\; export reads -14 LUFS / -1.0 dBTP.\n\nRIGHT LOOKS 
 LIKE\n- Chain proven AND a disconnect/rejoin + degraded-guest + CFR-tran
 scode rehearsed. Lip-sync clean at the end.\n\nHOW-TO GUIDES (plain lang
 uage\, jargon decoded\, each with a chatbot prompt)\n- Recording in Rive
 rside: https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/blob/main/how-t
 o/riverside-record.md\n- Editing + export numbers: https://github.com/rw
 smith96/mechanisms-in-motion/blob/main/how-to/descript-edit.md\n- All gu
 ides: https://github.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/blob/main/how-to
 /README.md\n\nASSISTANT PROMPT (paste into Claude or ChatGPT for step-by
 -step help)\nYou are helping run Mechanisms in Motion\, the AES podcast:
  a remote\, two-host video interview show that turns Amazon's internal o
 perating mechanisms into playbooks any company can use (tagline 'Day 1 E
 nergy for Every Stage of Growth'). Rich owns logistics\; Carla owns the 
 guest slate. Today's step: Prove the whole chain AND rehearse the real f
 ailure modes before the first marquee guest. Costs nothing to break here
 . WHAT TO DO: (1) Rich + Carla + a stand-in on a RANDOM laptop with a de
 fault webcam (rehearse the degraded guest\, not the happy path). (2) Mid
 -record\, have the stand-in close the tab and rejoin\; confirm their loc
 al track survived. (3) Confirm every participant's tracks upload to 100%
 \; rehearse the fix for a guest whose camera recorded at an odd frame ra
 te (converting it to a steady 30fps\, called CFR / constant frame rate\;
  the descript-edit guide has the one-click fix). (4) Export to Descript\
 ; confirm each person lands as a SEPARATE track\; verify lip-sync at the
  END of the take. (5) Confirm 30fps everywhere\; export reads -14 LUFS /
  -1.0 dBTP. DONE WHEN: Chain proven AND a disconnect/rejoin + degraded-g
 uest + CFR-transcode rehearsed. Lip-sync clean at the end.. YOUR TASK: W
 e are at STEP 7: full test run. Give me a 10-minute test-run script that
  deliberately rehearses a degraded guest\, a mid-record disconnect/rejoi
 n\, and the transcode-to-CFR fix\, plus a pass/fail checklist for the ch
 ain (100% upload\, separate-track export\, end-of-take lip-sync\, -14 LU
 FS / -1.0 dBTP\, 30fps)\, and exactly what to do if any check fails.\n\n
 FULL PROJECT SPEC (optional\, for deep context): https://raw.githubuserc
 ontent.com/rwsmith96/mechanisms-in-motion/main/mim-assistant-context.md
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
